# Testing Standards

## Framework

- Frontend: Jest + React Testing Library
- Run: `yarn test`

## File Structure

```
component/
├── MyComponent.tsx
└── MyComponent.test.tsx    # Co-located tests

functions/
└── myFunction/
    ├── index.js
    └── __tests__/
        └── myFunction.test.js
```

## Basic Test Pattern

```typescript
import { render, screen, fireEvent, waitFor } from '@testing-library/react';
import { MockedProvider } from '@apollo/client/testing';

jest.mock('next-auth/react');
jest.mock('next-intl', () => ({
  useTranslations: () => (key: string) => key,
}));

describe('MyComponent', () => {
  beforeEach(() => {
    jest.clearAllMocks();
  });

  it('renders correctly', () => {
    render(<MyComponent id={1} />);
    expect(screen.getByText('Expected')).toBeInTheDocument();
  });

  it('handles interactions', async () => {
    render(<MyComponent id={1} />);
    fireEvent.click(screen.getByRole('button'));
    await waitFor(() => expect(screen.getByText('Result')).toBeInTheDocument());
  });
});
```

## GraphQL Mocking

```typescript
const mocks = [{
  request: { query: MY_QUERY, variables: { id: 1 } },
  result: { data: { item: { id: 1, title: 'Test' } } },
}];

render(
  <MockedProvider mocks={mocks} addTypename={false}>
    <MyComponent id={1} />
  </MockedProvider>
);
```

## Key Rules

- ✅ Test behavior, not implementation
- ✅ Use `screen.getByRole` over `getByTestId`
- ✅ Mock external dependencies (GraphQL, auth)
- ✅ Clean up mocks in `beforeEach`/`afterEach`
- ❌ Don't test implementation details
